<p>French-Palestinian member of the European Parliament Rima Hassan is due to stand trial in France after prosecutors charged her over an X post that quoted or referred to a perpetrator of the 1972 Lod Airport attack in Israel. If convicted, she could face up to seven years in prison. Hassan says the case amounts to judicial and political harassment, while French authorities are pursuing it under laws that bar glorifying or promoting terrorism online. The case has become part of a broader debate in France over where political speech, advocacy for Palestinians, and criminal law tied to terrorism-related expression meet. Its significance is both legal and political: Hassan is an elected European lawmaker, and the proceedings will test how French courts apply anti-terror laws to social media speech by a high-profile public figure.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/D0w6CSQ1G1AyoN3bnEf3Cp8_yW2_nZXR-ANLWvaDS_qDdEP7IToW2nfc7aWvaEZ4ZffKChjqo-GKGurszIpJl0mQQUzk48bNkiVigoarwI9Rw38i-I8BOqdaQcVo_dlpYz5a8BWnQ5_sqYSu7cvqUfhk08jaE8NNR3jcxS8TxPmGvsTlaStZ91HzXeEJSsE94ebIHOxj' alt='Rima Hassan, center, and her lawyer Vincent Brengarth, left, after a hearing in Paris on Friday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Possible penalty: The charge described by The New York Times could leave Hassan facing up to seven years in prison if she is convicted, showing how seriously France treats online statements linked to terrorism cases.</li><li>1972 reference: The post at the center of the case referred to a Japanese man involved in the 1972 attack in Israel, an event that anchors the prosecution&#x27;s claim that the message glorified terrorism.</li><li>Parliament role: Hassan serves in the European Parliament, which gives the case added visibility because it concerns the speech of an elected EU legislator rather than a private citizen.</li><li>Public response: After a hearing in Paris, Hassan denounced the proceedings as harassment, signaling that she plans to challenge both the legal case and the political framing around it.</li></ul><blockquote>Genuine judicial and political harassment - Rima Hassan</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Rima Hassan: Hassan says she is facing judicial and political harassment, not a fair prosecution, and frames the case as part of a broader effort to target her activism and public positions. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/4/european-parliaments-rima-hassan-im-a-target-of-political'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>French prosecutors: Prosecutors are treating the social media post as a possible case of promoting or glorifying terrorism, using criminal law against online speech they say crossed a legal line. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/03/rima-hassan-france-terrorism-charges.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Le Monde analysis: Le Monde presents the case as part of growing tensions in France around Palestine-related speech, where legal scrutiny and political debate increasingly overlap. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/france/article/2026/04/04/french-palestinian-mep-rima-hassan-denounces-judicial-harassment-as-court-case-looms-over-social-media-post_6752107_7.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/france/article/2026/04/04/french-palestinian-mep-rima-hassan-denounces-judicial-harassment-as-court-case-looms-over-social-media-post_6752107_7.html'>French-Palestinian MEP Rima Hassan denounces &#x27;judicial harassment&#x27; as court case looms over social media post</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/4/european-parliaments-rima-hassan-im-a-target-of-political'>European Parliament’s Rima Hassan: I’m a target of ‘political harassment’</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/03/rima-hassan-france-terrorism-charges.html'>Rima Hassan Is Charged With Glorifying Terrorism Online in Social Media Post</a> - nytimes.com</li></ul>